    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d287">

                <pb facs="0287" n="171" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg171"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 893.00/1217.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the American
                        Minister</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-04-04">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 4, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have to enclose herewith for the
                    information and guidance of the Legation copy of an instruction this day
                    addressed to the <pb facs="0288" n="172" xml:id="pg172"/> Consul General at
                    Hankow regarding the manner of treating claims of American citizens and firms
                    growing out of the recent disturbances in China.</p>
                <p>In replying to any requests on the part of the American consular officers in
                    China for instructions as to what action, if any, they may properly take with
                    reference to such claims, you should follow the instructions embodied in the
                    inclosure to this communication.</p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Huntington Wilson.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d287-a1.xml" xpointer="d287-a1"/>
            </div>
